# Migration Contract

A hosting, deployment, path, runtime, or infrastructure migration preserves
the existing product contract unless the user explicitly approves a product
change.

- Do not add user-managed keys, accounts, billing, quota exposure, setup
  steps, paid services, or new runtime dependencies as part of a migration.
- Do not replace a working capability merely because another implementation
  is more official, modern, or architecturally attractive.
- Separate migration work from redesign proposals. Describe any proposed
  behavior or dependency change and obtain approval before implementing it.
- Before shipping, compare old and new user-visible requirements, external
  dependencies, URLs, persistence, and failure behavior.
- Test the preserved end-to-end user path, not only infrastructure health.

Example: moving keyless music search to a new host must remain keyless. A
browser YouTube API key is a product redesign, not migration work.
